{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Batch versus Stream Processing.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Batch versus Stream Processing.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"batch versus stream processing batch versus stream processing","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Batch versus Stream Processing.md","fileName":"Batch versus Stream Processing.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Batch versus Stream Processing","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-15 09:13\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Data Science Infrastructure and Integration]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Data Science Infrastructure and Integration","datascience_mit.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Batch versus Stream Processing.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Batch versus Stream Processing.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"batch versus stream processing batch versus stream processing","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Batch versus Stream Processing.md","fileName":"Batch versus Stream Processing.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Batch versus Stream Processing","heading":"Batch versus Stream Processing","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Batch processing applies an operation to a dataset whose results are not urgently required. Stream processing handles each arriving element as it enters a system, making it suitable for time-sensitive labels, alerts, or measurements. The choice changes both the unit of computation and the latency the architecture must support.\n\nThe book contrasts Hadoop's batch-oriented approach with Storm's stream-oriented approach and describes Spark and Flink as combining capabilities. The general design question is not which platform name is fashionable, but whether the task needs a historical aggregate, a prompt response to each event, or both.","tags":["baby"],"lin